WEBVTT

00:27.000 --> 00:27.840
[sighs]

00:31.480 --> 00:32.360
[liquid sloshing]

01:09.120 --> 01:11.120
[phone ringing]

01:30.320 --> 01:35.920
♪ Mmm, pacify ♪

01:39.800 --> 01:43.240
♪ Clarify our love ♪

01:46.360 --> 01:48.920
♪ Pacify, pacify ♪

01:55.040 --> 01:57.720
♪ Pacify, pacify ♪

01:59.640 --> 02:01.960
♪ Pacify our love ♪

02:32.400 --> 02:33.920
[clock ticking]

02:37.240 --> 02:38.280
[metal clicks]

03:25.200 --> 03:26.360
[exhales heavily]

04:30.960 --> 04:32.320
[exhales sharply]

04:32.400 --> 04:36.040
[Charlie in distance]
Dad, there's a phone call for ya!

04:41.400 --> 04:44.280
Dad, there's a phone call for ya!

04:46.080 --> 04:47.160
[Tommy] Charlie!

04:48.960 --> 04:49.840
Charlie!

04:50.920 --> 04:52.960
Wait! Charlie!

05:05.520 --> 05:06.960
[Tommy panting]

05:09.160 --> 05:11.080
Giddy-up, horsey! Giddy-up!

05:17.560 --> 05:19.640
Dad, there's a phone call for ya.

05:20.400 --> 05:22.920
[breathing heavily] Good boy. Good boy.

05:23.000 --> 05:24.760
Well, you go back to the house,

05:24.840 --> 05:29.680
and whoever's calling,
the operator will have their number,

05:29.760 --> 05:31.760
and I'll call them back. Eh?

05:31.840 --> 05:33.520
[vehicle approaching]

05:35.360 --> 05:38.520
Oh, look, Charlie,
you must have violin practice.

05:38.600 --> 05:41.440
It's Mrs Milligan. Go on. [sniffles]

05:42.400 --> 05:45.840
Charlie. Charlie, you play loudly!

05:46.400 --> 05:47.960
You might hear some bangs.

05:49.640 --> 05:50.720
Go on.

06:04.240 --> 06:05.080
[exhales heavily]

06:15.840 --> 06:17.440
[violin playing]

07:30.640 --> 07:32.320
[breathing heavily]

07:39.840 --> 07:40.760
[line beeps]

07:41.440 --> 07:43.000
-[button clicks]
-[line ringing]

07:43.080 --> 07:44.320
[Maggie] Hi, Mr Shelby.

07:44.400 --> 07:46.600
[breathing heavily] Maggie? Yeah, it's me.

07:46.680 --> 07:49.960
-Yes, Mr Shelby.
-I just missed a call. Where was it from?

07:50.040 --> 07:50.920
Er, Belfast.

07:52.080 --> 07:53.440
Belfast.

07:54.280 --> 07:55.720
Where in Belfast?

07:55.800 --> 07:57.280
Er, I'm not sure.

07:57.360 --> 07:58.440
Do you have the number?

07:58.920 --> 08:00.160
-Yes.
-Yeah.

08:00.240 --> 08:02.520
It's 0-8-24.

08:03.560 --> 08:05.080
Yeah, can you put me through?

08:05.160 --> 08:07.040
[static over phone]

08:10.240 --> 08:11.640
[line ringing]

08:13.040 --> 08:13.880
[Michael] Tommy. Don't--

08:15.560 --> 08:16.760
[footsteps approaching]

08:19.800 --> 08:20.960
Mr Shelby.

08:21.680 --> 08:25.520
My name is Captain Swing,
calling from the occupied six counties.

08:26.200 --> 08:27.280
And there are some people

08:27.360 --> 08:31.200
from the other side of our
neat little city that want you dead.

08:31.880 --> 08:34.360
[Swing] You should also know
that this boy,

08:34.440 --> 08:37.159
this Michael, your kin,

08:37.720 --> 08:40.880
was in his cabin aboard
the SS Monroe in Belfast dock,

08:40.960 --> 08:43.880
making deals with the very men
who want you dead.

08:43.960 --> 08:45.960
-Tommy, they're lying!
-Now, if you want,

08:46.039 --> 08:48.520
we can put a bullet in his head,
here and now,

08:49.400 --> 08:51.920
or we can send him home,
and you can deal with him.

08:57.880 --> 08:59.200
Send him home.

09:00.720 --> 09:02.240
Very well, Mr Shelby.

09:02.840 --> 09:05.560
But be informed that this kin of yours

09:05.640 --> 09:09.880
was talking to representatives from
the County Tyrone and Glasgow UVF

09:09.960 --> 09:12.440
about how they'd divide up
the English racetracks

09:12.520 --> 09:14.040
after they'd blown away your legs.

09:14.120 --> 09:15.680
Tommy, they're lying!

09:18.040 --> 09:19.240
And may I ask...

09:20.680 --> 09:22.400
why you are doing me this favour?

09:25.320 --> 09:29.560
Because, Mr Shelby, we've been informed
by people at the very highest level

09:30.160 --> 09:32.680
that since your conversion to socialism,

09:32.760 --> 09:34.640
you're now on the side of the angels.

09:35.680 --> 09:37.800
And angels can be useful to us.

09:40.000 --> 09:41.040
[line disconnects]

09:59.240 --> 10:00.320
[footsteps approaching]

10:00.400 --> 10:01.480
[knocking at door]

10:04.560 --> 10:05.600
-Come.
-[door opens]

10:06.560 --> 10:07.720
[footsteps approaching]

10:14.200 --> 10:17.800
Mr Shelby, the violin teacher
wants to know what all those bangs were.

10:19.240 --> 10:21.800
Fireworks. I was trying 'em out
for Saturday.

10:25.360 --> 10:27.720
You promised the doctor
not until after dark.

10:28.240 --> 10:29.120
[scoffs]

10:29.200 --> 10:31.000
It's pretty dark, Frances.

10:34.320 --> 10:38.880
Also, will Mrs Shelby and Ruby
be home for dinner tonight?

10:38.960 --> 10:40.200
I don't know.

10:46.720 --> 10:47.760
[footsteps approaching]

10:50.080 --> 10:51.160
[Charlie] Dad?

10:52.400 --> 10:54.560
I've learned something this morning.

10:54.640 --> 10:55.560
[Tommy] Have ya?

10:58.720 --> 10:59.720
So have I.

11:01.240 --> 11:02.960
And what have you learned, my boy?

11:05.280 --> 11:06.560
[Charlie playing violin]

11:26.160 --> 11:28.480
[Tommy] Let's get this over with.
I've got a train to catch.

11:28.560 --> 11:30.960
Go get your train, Tom.
I can deal with this.

11:31.040 --> 11:32.200
Hey!

11:32.880 --> 11:34.320
[indistinct chatter]

11:39.760 --> 11:40.640
[door closes]

11:42.200 --> 11:44.200
-[floorboards creaking]
-[glass crunching]

11:51.600 --> 11:52.520
[stool dragging]

11:54.600 --> 11:55.440
Go home.

11:55.520 --> 11:56.360
[gasps]

11:58.320 --> 11:59.480
[Arthur] Come here, you.

12:00.360 --> 12:01.320
Put this on.

12:02.280 --> 12:06.080
There you go. Look at that.
Looks great on ya! Wrap up warm.

12:17.880 --> 12:19.600
[exclaims and breathes heavily]

12:19.680 --> 12:20.760
[Arthur] Wake up.

12:21.920 --> 12:23.200
Rise and shine.

12:24.320 --> 12:25.520
What are you doing here?

12:25.600 --> 12:27.000
Wasting our fucking time on you.

12:27.080 --> 12:28.440
[groans]

12:31.680 --> 12:33.080
[Tommy] Sit down, Finn.

12:34.080 --> 12:35.160
Sit down.

12:42.280 --> 12:43.480
What do I have to do...

12:44.920 --> 12:46.880
to make you fucking listen to me?

12:48.120 --> 12:49.360
You took a bullet.

12:50.080 --> 12:52.800
You've been running around the streets
with a fucking gun in your hand.

12:54.880 --> 12:56.280
Somebody has to.

12:59.000 --> 13:01.320
Finn, we've got people
for that kind of work.

13:01.400 --> 13:04.400
Soldiers. Captains and corporals.

13:05.200 --> 13:06.320
Well, then, what am I?

13:07.760 --> 13:09.360
"What am I?" Jesus Christ. [clears throat]

13:09.440 --> 13:11.240
[Finn] Yeah. What am I, Tom? Huh?

13:12.360 --> 13:14.400
I'm the brother you never got around to.

13:16.080 --> 13:17.680
[Tommy] You're a general, Finn.

13:18.560 --> 13:22.360
You understand? You're a fucking Shelby,
so you're a general.

13:22.440 --> 13:26.320
When did you last see a general
anywhere near the blood and the puke, eh?

13:27.960 --> 13:29.520
[Arthur] He's fucking right.

13:30.040 --> 13:31.440
That's what you are.

13:31.920 --> 13:33.360
So, on your feet, soldier.

13:34.520 --> 13:36.000
Come on, on your feet!

13:36.080 --> 13:38.080
I thought you just said I was a general.

13:38.960 --> 13:40.840
I did just say you were.

13:40.920 --> 13:43.240
-So, get on your fucking feet--
-Arthur.

13:43.920 --> 13:47.680
Finn. Finn. Look at this.

13:47.760 --> 13:51.400
This is the bullet
that Aberama Gold cut from you.

13:51.960 --> 13:53.480
First and last.

13:56.480 --> 13:57.480
First and last.

14:01.440 --> 14:02.680
[Finn sighs]

14:03.360 --> 14:04.560
Don't lose it.

14:05.840 --> 14:07.320
Go and clean up.

14:07.400 --> 14:09.720
Put some clothes on. Nice suit.

14:10.360 --> 14:12.560
I've got some trouble
that'll keep you out of trouble.

14:15.200 --> 14:17.360
-Oh, and, er, Tom...
-Yeah?

14:17.440 --> 14:19.200
[Finn] While you're here, erm,

14:19.880 --> 14:21.440
I've met this girl,
and I'd like to get married.

14:21.520 --> 14:23.000
Fuck off. Go, get dressed.

14:23.080 --> 14:24.240
Go on. Move.

14:24.320 --> 14:25.160
Go!

14:25.640 --> 14:27.520
[Tommy] Finn, this girl
you're trying to impress...

14:27.600 --> 14:28.960
Tell me about her.

14:30.080 --> 14:31.640
She likes the life.

14:31.720 --> 14:33.280
[Tommy] She likes the life, eh?

14:33.800 --> 14:35.400
Well, find one that hates it.

14:35.480 --> 14:38.240
Look at him. That's what he did,
and now he's chairman of the board.

14:39.360 --> 14:40.200
[Arthur grunts]

14:41.120 --> 14:42.440
Go on. Hurry up.

14:43.560 --> 14:45.960
[Tommy] Arthur? Lizzie and Ruby...

14:46.920 --> 14:48.400
are they still at yours?

14:51.240 --> 14:52.760
Yes, Tom, they're still there.

14:53.440 --> 14:55.520
She's coming home today, she said, so...

14:56.040 --> 14:57.440
She'll be home later.

14:58.320 --> 15:00.760
Hmm. Has she been talking about me?

15:01.400 --> 15:04.120
I mean, they talk a lot.
You know what women are like.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.960
The kitchen and... You know?

15:06.040 --> 15:09.120
Kids running around.
I don't pay 'em no mind, Tom.

15:09.200 --> 15:11.800
-I don't listen to 'em half the time.
-[Tommy] Yeah.

15:12.320 --> 15:14.120
Well, everything she says is true.

15:18.400 --> 15:19.360
Well...

15:21.880 --> 15:25.080
-You like the life, Tommy.
-I don't like the fucking life.

15:25.160 --> 15:26.720
I don't like the fucking life.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.440
I don't like that
Michael is coming back today.

15:32.720 --> 15:34.840
Train arrives from Liverpool at 3:00.

15:34.920 --> 15:37.360
Polly will be there. Take a weapon.

15:38.680 --> 15:42.160
Tell Moss to clear the station of coppers,
you hear me?

15:42.240 --> 15:43.520
Yes, sir.

15:45.840 --> 15:46.840
Hey, Tom...

15:49.480 --> 15:51.040
I heard 'em say one thing, though.

15:52.680 --> 15:55.240
Just talking, you know?
They were saying that, er...

15:55.880 --> 15:58.320
[hesitantly] you don't sleep,
or something.

15:59.800 --> 16:01.120
You can't sleep.

16:01.200 --> 16:02.960
[breathes deeply]

16:03.040 --> 16:04.560
When I do sleep,

16:05.480 --> 16:06.600
I dream.

16:07.480 --> 16:08.840
And in my dream,

16:09.840 --> 16:12.400
someone wants my crown. [smacks lips]

16:12.480 --> 16:13.920
Think it might be Michael.

16:14.760 --> 16:16.000
Call me at 3:00.

16:22.680 --> 16:23.680
[door closes]

16:23.760 --> 16:27.440
[Finn] Arthur, I'm gonna put that bullet
on a necklace and wear it as a reminder.

16:28.120 --> 16:29.160
Arthur?

16:29.960 --> 16:31.800
-I heard ya.
-You got trouble for me, then?

16:32.480 --> 16:33.920
-Yeah.
-Yeah?

16:40.520 --> 16:42.640
-[footsteps approaching]
-[indistinct chatter]

16:48.920 --> 16:51.600
Mr Shelby... Er... Er...
The police are here to see you.

16:51.680 --> 16:52.960
Police aren't allowed in here.

16:53.040 --> 16:56.160
Er... He's not in uniform
and said it's very unofficial.

16:57.880 --> 16:58.720
[door closes]

16:59.720 --> 17:00.880
[footsteps approaching]

17:01.640 --> 17:04.000
Afternoon. Someone get you some tea?

17:04.080 --> 17:05.360
[Stacker] No, I'm fine, Mr Shelby.

17:05.440 --> 17:06.760
-This won't take long.
-[Tommy] Good.

17:07.960 --> 17:09.240
You got five minutes.

17:10.880 --> 17:11.960
Mr Shelby,

17:12.800 --> 17:16.200
there was a shooting two days ago.
A man died.

17:16.760 --> 17:18.079
It was a murder.

17:19.960 --> 17:21.200
In Maida Vale,

17:21.800 --> 17:23.400
[chuckles softly] of all places.

17:26.480 --> 17:28.160
-His name was Levitt.
-Uh-huh.

17:30.640 --> 17:31.920
He was a journalist.

17:43.160 --> 17:46.040
The night before he was shot,
he came here to see you.

17:47.640 --> 17:50.520
We found a Commons pass
and your name in his diary.

17:51.360 --> 17:54.280
I was wondering
what his business here was.

17:56.560 --> 17:57.800
And I'm wondering...

17:59.000 --> 18:00.560
what your business here is.

18:00.640 --> 18:01.480
[scoffs]

18:02.680 --> 18:05.280
According to his diary,
you knew him from Birmingham.

18:05.360 --> 18:06.360
What's your name?

18:08.360 --> 18:10.920
-Stacker.
-Stacker. Okay.

18:13.440 --> 18:15.840
Mr Shelby, Mr Levitt was a queer.

18:16.840 --> 18:18.720
Some may think
it was one of his queer friends.

18:18.800 --> 18:20.280
Mr Stacker,

18:20.840 --> 18:23.800
I get the feeling
that with a little provocation,

18:24.440 --> 18:25.920
you could be very persistent.

18:27.120 --> 18:28.280
Only within my remit.

18:28.360 --> 18:30.600
Well, your Chief Constable Wyatt,

18:30.680 --> 18:34.720
he has very clear views about persistence
which he has shared with me.

18:34.800 --> 18:36.840
-Mr Shelby--
-He likes persistence,

18:36.920 --> 18:38.680
as do I, and thoroughness.

18:39.520 --> 18:40.760
But not frivolity.

18:42.360 --> 18:45.440
A man who walks in the park with other men

18:46.080 --> 18:47.960
dies in Maida Vale. [chuckles]

18:48.640 --> 18:50.080
And you come to me?

18:50.800 --> 18:52.040
As well as his diary,

18:52.600 --> 18:54.360
-we have his notebook.
-[bell ringing]

18:56.960 --> 18:59.320
Your time's up, Mr Stacker.

19:05.440 --> 19:06.760
[footsteps receding]

19:08.080 --> 19:09.120
Thank you.

19:12.480 --> 19:13.320
[door opens]

19:14.360 --> 19:15.200
[door closes]

19:16.360 --> 19:21.040
♪ You have no idea what I'm capable of ♪

19:27.600 --> 19:32.520
♪ You have never tasted
This kind of love ♪

19:39.000 --> 19:43.880
♪ Underestimate me and see how it goes ♪

19:44.600 --> 19:47.040
♪ Love you to death ♪

19:49.480 --> 19:50.320
[Michael] Hello, Mum!

19:53.240 --> 19:54.400
This is Gina.

19:56.120 --> 19:57.240
Gina Gray.

19:58.960 --> 20:00.840
The captain married us on board.

20:03.680 --> 20:05.640
She's my wife, Mum.
At least look at her.

20:05.720 --> 20:09.640
Tommy said to ask you
to tell me the truth.

20:10.440 --> 20:12.800
We've been travelling
for 15 days, Mrs Gray.

20:12.880 --> 20:14.680
Maybe we could talk about this
at another time?

20:14.760 --> 20:16.920
Yes. Let's go home and we can talk.

20:17.000 --> 20:20.920
You have no home
until you tell me the truth.

20:22.480 --> 20:23.920
-Here?
-Yeah.

20:27.920 --> 20:28.880
[Arthur] Michael!

20:32.280 --> 20:33.520
Hello, love.

20:34.840 --> 20:36.920
Welcome to Birmingham, eh.

20:39.040 --> 20:40.160
Michael.

20:42.480 --> 20:43.480
Okay.

20:46.280 --> 20:48.200
Our ship docked at Belfast.

20:48.280 --> 20:50.640
-I was then taken off the ship by two men.
-At gunpoint--

20:50.720 --> 20:52.800
I'm speaking to my son.

20:52.880 --> 20:53.960
Fuck you.

20:55.680 --> 20:57.280
Fuck you, too, Arthur!

20:58.040 --> 20:59.640
This is my fucking wife.

20:59.720 --> 21:01.720
I'm bringing her home, to this.

21:03.520 --> 21:04.640
[scoffs]

21:04.720 --> 21:06.040
Come on, Gina.

21:10.360 --> 21:12.720
Well, where are you going now, eh? Hmm?

21:13.280 --> 21:14.680
Introduce me, at least.

21:14.760 --> 21:16.360
-Excuse me.
-Look at this.

21:17.320 --> 21:18.600
Look at this.

21:19.120 --> 21:20.520
This is it, Gina.

21:21.280 --> 21:23.760
This is my fuckin' people.

21:24.720 --> 21:26.360
Do you wanna know the truth, Arthur?

21:27.000 --> 21:28.760
Do you wanna know the truth, Mum?

21:29.560 --> 21:34.360
I did not betray my fucking family!

21:36.120 --> 21:38.160
Now, Mum,

21:39.520 --> 21:40.880
I want to go home.

21:43.280 --> 21:45.840
[Polly] I've booked you a suite
at the Midland Hotel.

21:46.720 --> 21:48.640
[Michael] Was that Tommy's orders,
then, was it?

21:49.440 --> 21:52.680
See, the Midland Hotel
is Tommy's little kingdom,

21:53.760 --> 21:56.160
where all the porters keep an eye,

21:57.080 --> 22:00.400
where all the telephone exchange girls
are reporting on my calls.

22:00.480 --> 22:03.600
Yeah, well, why don't you
think of it like, er...

22:04.120 --> 22:05.960
quarantine, Michael, eh?

22:07.320 --> 22:10.480
We treat you like a fucking dog. Hmm?

22:12.240 --> 22:15.240
Smelly one, stinking one,

22:16.120 --> 22:19.160
until we know you're clean.

22:19.800 --> 22:20.760
Hmm?

22:20.840 --> 22:22.920
-Fuck you, Arthur.
-[chuckles]

22:23.000 --> 22:24.440
Stand aside, Arthur.

22:25.160 --> 22:26.640
No, Pol.

22:34.360 --> 22:36.400
Come on, baby. Forget about it.

22:37.440 --> 22:39.160
Go and phone Tommy.

22:39.240 --> 22:40.520
Tell him,

22:40.600 --> 22:43.560
"Polly says Michael's telling the truth."

22:44.120 --> 22:46.080
[Gina] It's all right. Forget about it.

22:46.160 --> 22:47.320
All right, Pol.

22:50.320 --> 22:51.880
[Arthur] Nice coat.

22:51.960 --> 22:53.880
What are you, like, a camel, right?

22:56.840 --> 22:57.800
Oh.

22:59.520 --> 23:02.480
Welcome to the family, Gina Gray.

23:06.880 --> 23:10.560
[Tommy] I applaud the attempt
in the Trevelyan Education Bill

23:10.640 --> 23:13.240
to raise the school-leaving age to 15.

23:15.880 --> 23:19.360
♪ All these folk
They think that I'm evil ♪

23:19.440 --> 23:24.160
♪ Like I am the living devil himself ♪

23:24.240 --> 23:27.920
♪ All these folk
They think that I'm evil ♪

23:28.000 --> 23:31.000
♪ Like I am the living devil ♪

23:31.080 --> 23:33.200
[Tommy] ...as regards means
testing of any kind,

23:33.280 --> 23:35.600
-we are the people.
-[crowd agreeing]

23:35.680 --> 23:36.560
We've had enough.

23:36.640 --> 23:37.800
[crowd] Hear, hear!

23:38.760 --> 23:41.200
"We are the people and we've had enough."

23:41.280 --> 23:42.880
[Tommy] I move in favour of the amendment.

23:47.160 --> 23:48.840
[indistinct chatter and laughter]

23:58.920 --> 24:00.240
Mr Shelby.

24:01.600 --> 24:04.920
I must say,
you sing like a songbird in the House.

24:05.000 --> 24:05.880
[inhales sharply]

24:06.840 --> 24:09.880
-And who is this pretty finch?
-My sister.

24:09.960 --> 24:13.240
-Who's pregnant.
-And dangerous. [clears throat]

24:13.320 --> 24:15.400
Oh, we adore dangerous.

24:15.480 --> 24:16.680
Who's "we"?

24:16.760 --> 24:18.840
It's a collective noun.

24:18.920 --> 24:22.600
In this case, describing a group of people
who are impatient and young

24:22.680 --> 24:25.600
and, as I have said, adore dangerous.

24:27.680 --> 24:31.320
Mr Shelby, you had a horse of that name.

24:32.400 --> 24:34.360
Whiskey, Irish.

24:35.040 --> 24:36.840
Give him one from my bottle,

24:36.920 --> 24:38.240
and one for myself.

24:38.320 --> 24:39.800
In fact, bring the bottle.

24:40.560 --> 24:41.400
And the lady?

24:42.040 --> 24:44.720
Isn't thirsty.
How'd you know about the horse?

24:46.680 --> 24:48.640
We have a mutual acquaintance.

24:50.080 --> 24:50.920
May Carleton.

24:51.480 --> 24:55.120
When I asked about you, she said,
"Oh, my goodness, where do I begin?"

24:56.720 --> 24:58.640
And why were you asking after me?

24:59.320 --> 25:02.440
Because, as I have said,
I adore dangerous.

25:04.480 --> 25:05.920
And where did she begin?

25:06.640 --> 25:08.960
You know, I was rather hoping
we might have this meeting alone.

25:09.880 --> 25:12.000
My sister is my political advisor.

25:12.080 --> 25:15.000
And my advice just now was,
"Don't meet Mr Mosley."

25:15.560 --> 25:16.920
Because I am dangerous?

25:17.000 --> 25:18.120
[Tommy] No.

25:19.480 --> 25:21.680
What is it
you are impatient for, Mr Mosley?

25:22.960 --> 25:25.680
I'm impatient for my fucking whiskey.

25:28.040 --> 25:29.240
Bennet!

25:30.240 --> 25:31.160
[scoffs]

25:32.560 --> 25:33.760
[Mosley] May Carleton spoke about you

25:33.840 --> 25:37.680
the way I imagine one might
about a party they barely remember,

25:37.760 --> 25:40.760
where you crash the car into the dovecote

25:40.840 --> 25:44.040
and live on champagne and cocaine
for three whole days.

25:44.120 --> 25:45.520
You know that kind of party?

25:45.600 --> 25:47.200
Only three days?

25:49.160 --> 25:50.080
[chuckles]

25:54.160 --> 25:57.320
My sister advised against meeting you

25:57.880 --> 25:59.040
because it appears

25:59.800 --> 26:01.800
you are moving away from the party...

26:03.600 --> 26:05.480
in a different direction.

26:05.560 --> 26:07.120
And which direction is that?

26:07.880 --> 26:09.600
Towards fascism.

26:11.000 --> 26:14.240
"We are the people
and we have had enough."

26:16.680 --> 26:18.480
I thought that was excellent.

26:19.320 --> 26:21.960
In which direction
are you heading, Mr Shelby?

26:23.680 --> 26:25.440
I am my own revolution.

26:26.040 --> 26:28.480
And you prefer Irish to Scotch.

26:30.480 --> 26:31.760
As do I.

26:31.840 --> 26:36.240
Like all things regarding Ireland,
it is complex, yes?

26:44.120 --> 26:44.960
Oh.

26:46.480 --> 26:49.480
Where do you stand
on the Irish Question, Mr Shelby?

26:51.000 --> 26:52.320
Never been asked it.

26:52.400 --> 26:54.640
Then perhaps it's time you were.

26:55.720 --> 26:59.240
Tommy, I am the people,
and I have had enough.

26:59.760 --> 27:02.240
[Mosley] We're looking for someone
to begin a dialogue

27:02.320 --> 27:04.680
with certain elements in Belfast

27:04.760 --> 27:07.600
with whom we don't officially
have any dealings.

27:08.920 --> 27:11.160
I'll be too busy singing in the House.

27:12.200 --> 27:13.880
It would involve a promotion.

27:15.080 --> 27:17.840
Junior minister to the Duchy of Lancaster.

27:19.840 --> 27:21.720
Birmingham is my concern.

27:21.800 --> 27:22.680
Ireland bores me.

27:23.280 --> 27:25.800
Thanks for the whiskey, Mr Mosley.

27:33.400 --> 27:34.240
[chuckles]

27:35.800 --> 27:37.440
What the fuck was that about?

27:37.520 --> 27:40.680
Ireland. It's been Ireland's day
all fucking day long.

27:40.760 --> 27:41.800
What do you mean?

27:41.880 --> 27:43.320
Ada, go home

27:43.400 --> 27:46.600
and start calling anyone who had dealings
with Shelby Company Limited

27:46.680 --> 27:48.000
while you were in Boston.

27:48.080 --> 27:49.480
Ask 'em about Michael.

27:51.320 --> 27:52.800
Ask them what about him?

27:52.880 --> 27:54.000
Who he's been seeing,

27:54.080 --> 27:55.480
who he's been meeting,

27:55.560 --> 27:56.960
what deals he's made.

27:57.040 --> 27:58.240
Why?

27:58.320 --> 28:02.480
Ask 'em especially about people
he's met from Glasgow or Belfast.

28:03.200 --> 28:06.520
Tommy, why don't you
come back with me, huh?

28:06.600 --> 28:08.240
You can play chess with Karl.

28:08.320 --> 28:10.880
I'll make some calls, you can listen in.
Drive home tomorrow--

28:10.960 --> 28:12.880
Then that bastard

28:12.960 --> 28:16.040
starts talking about Irish whiskey.
What the fuck does he know, eh?

28:16.120 --> 28:18.320
More than me, Tommy.
What are you talking about?

28:18.920 --> 28:21.840
I'm talking about an empty chair, Ada.

28:21.920 --> 28:24.080
My chair. My throne.

28:24.160 --> 28:25.720
People think that I'm gonna fall.

28:25.800 --> 28:28.320
They start behaving
in a different way around here.

28:28.400 --> 28:29.560
Who thinks that?

28:30.320 --> 28:31.880
They start to circle.

28:32.520 --> 28:34.000
Who's gonna take the throne, eh?

28:34.640 --> 28:36.520
Linda, she wants some for Arthur...

28:36.600 --> 28:39.120
Aberama Gold,
people in the north, Michael...

28:40.160 --> 28:41.000
[clears throat]

28:44.040 --> 28:46.320
Just go home, make some calls.

28:46.960 --> 28:48.800
Protestants are coming, I think.

28:49.320 --> 28:51.000
I need to get back to Birmingham.

28:53.400 --> 28:54.240
[scoffs]

28:54.320 --> 28:55.200
[door closes]

29:04.440 --> 29:05.480
[Arthur] Polly.

29:06.200 --> 29:07.040
[Polly] You armed?

29:08.760 --> 29:09.760
Yeah.

29:10.880 --> 29:11.720
Yeah.

29:12.320 --> 29:14.240
Will you please consider
putting your weapons behind the bar,

29:14.320 --> 29:16.120
in case feelings begin to run high?

29:16.760 --> 29:18.200
Behind the bar, Pol, eh?

29:19.760 --> 29:21.280
Behind my own bar, yeah?

29:28.320 --> 29:29.840
I prefer it there.

29:32.480 --> 29:33.640
Thomas.

29:42.200 --> 29:43.320
[Tommy] Had a dream...

29:44.320 --> 29:46.720
about a black cat last night, Pol.

29:49.120 --> 29:50.400
A black cat dream

29:51.000 --> 29:54.240
means there is a traitor close by.
It was you who taught me that.

29:54.880 --> 29:56.880
[Polly] Black cat can mean lots of things.

29:57.920 --> 30:00.880
It can mean you're hurting yourself,
betraying yourself.

30:02.920 --> 30:04.280
Are you seeing things, Thomas?

30:04.360 --> 30:05.880
[vehicle approaching]

30:06.960 --> 30:08.240
Yes, I am.

30:09.760 --> 30:11.480
Yes, I am, very clearly.

30:13.920 --> 30:16.240
Coming from every fucking direction.

30:17.400 --> 30:18.520
[car engine stops]

30:20.960 --> 30:21.840
[car door closes]

30:24.160 --> 30:25.040
[bar door opens]

30:30.040 --> 30:31.080
Tommy.

30:32.760 --> 30:34.800
I'd like to introduce you to my wife.

30:36.560 --> 30:38.920
I would also like to, er, say something.

30:39.000 --> 30:40.080
Sit down, Michael.

30:40.840 --> 30:42.440
-I betrayed you.
-Michael.

30:42.520 --> 30:43.760
But only in my heart.

30:45.000 --> 30:47.240
There was a time, in America,

30:48.120 --> 30:50.240
when there was
a lot of money in that bank.

30:50.320 --> 30:51.800
And I wondered, I could...

30:51.880 --> 30:53.960
I could leave, move to California.

30:54.720 --> 30:57.000
Someone said I should invest in pictures.

30:57.760 --> 30:59.000
-Hollywood.
-[scoffs]

31:00.880 --> 31:02.240
But Gina stopped me.

31:03.280 --> 31:05.600
-Gina said that--
-I told you to sit down, Michael.

31:14.720 --> 31:15.800
Now tell me...

31:17.440 --> 31:19.120
what happened on that ship...

31:20.440 --> 31:21.760
in Belfast harbour.

31:24.360 --> 31:26.880
On the journey back from New York,
we got married.

31:27.680 --> 31:30.800
But we needed to find a witness, a purser.

31:31.520 --> 31:33.520
He was from Belfast. We got friendly.

31:33.600 --> 31:35.360
What happened when the ship docked?

31:37.400 --> 31:40.360
This purser had friends
who ran a whiskey distillery

31:40.440 --> 31:41.800
in County Tyrone.

31:41.880 --> 31:44.440
They wanted a way
of getting their stuff into America.

31:44.520 --> 31:46.480
So I said, "Okay, invite them aboard."

31:47.120 --> 31:50.440
When they came in,
I realized that they didn't make whiskey.

31:50.520 --> 31:52.880
They were Scottish, from Glasgow.

31:52.960 --> 31:55.600
Couldn't understand
a fucking word they were saying.

31:56.400 --> 31:59.560
They started swearing,
so I asked Gina to leave.

32:00.600 --> 32:02.760
That was when they
started talking about you, Tom.

32:03.920 --> 32:06.520
They said that Tommy Shelby
was a spent force.

32:07.880 --> 32:09.760
That politics had got to him.

32:10.880 --> 32:12.680
That he was spent in the head.

32:13.440 --> 32:17.480
That now was a good time to move in,
and did I want to be part of it?

32:18.400 --> 32:20.160
They knew about the money
we lost in America.

32:20.240 --> 32:22.040
They said that you were going to blame me,

32:22.120 --> 32:24.200
that you had a bullet with my name on it.

32:26.880 --> 32:28.440
What did you say, Michael?

32:28.520 --> 32:30.160
[Michael] I didn't have time
to say anything.

32:31.160 --> 32:32.720
Coppers came on board.

32:33.320 --> 32:35.320
Well, I thought they were coppers.
They, er...

32:36.760 --> 32:38.040
They were IRA.

32:38.840 --> 32:39.840
[Michael] Exactly.

32:45.720 --> 32:47.640
And the first men, from Glasgow?

32:50.280 --> 32:53.800
The IRA commander
said the men from Glasgow

32:53.880 --> 32:55.480
were called Billy Boys.

32:56.280 --> 32:58.120
Fucking Billy Boys.

32:58.200 --> 33:00.160
I don't know who the fuck Billy Boys are.

33:00.240 --> 33:02.280
They run every man

33:02.360 --> 33:05.720
in every coal mine,
on every shipyard east of Glasgow.

33:06.280 --> 33:11.760
Ties with Belfast, UVF.
Protestant razor gang.

33:12.360 --> 33:14.440
They also dabble in politics.

33:14.920 --> 33:19.160
You know, muscle for fascist rallies.

33:19.840 --> 33:21.440
[Polly] But you did no deal, Michael.

33:22.040 --> 33:24.080
You didn't even know who they were?

33:24.160 --> 33:26.840
I was too busy looking forward to
giving you the good news.

33:28.720 --> 33:32.280
The reason Gina and I got married
on the ship was because Gina is pregnant.

33:33.960 --> 33:35.640
You're going to be a grandmother.

33:44.200 --> 33:45.520
Okay, Michael.

33:47.120 --> 33:48.400
I believe you.

33:49.000 --> 33:50.160
Welcome home.

33:51.240 --> 33:52.520
Congratulations.

33:53.320 --> 33:54.560
Just remember...

33:55.920 --> 33:59.920
your unborn child
has witnessed what you said...

34:00.000 --> 34:01.360
Thomas.

34:01.440 --> 34:03.200
...and it will be born accordingly.

34:03.280 --> 34:05.760
-You fuck!
-Where the fuck are you going?

34:05.840 --> 34:06.680
Hmm?

34:07.160 --> 34:09.120
Are you fucking mad? Hmm?

34:11.800 --> 34:14.639
-You are free to fucking leave, Michael.
-[grunts]

34:14.719 --> 34:16.719
You fucking bastard.

34:16.800 --> 34:19.040
But you're not free, Michael, are you?

34:20.760 --> 34:23.080
You lost this company a lot of money.

34:23.159 --> 34:24.960
I told you to sell,

34:26.000 --> 34:27.440
but you held on.

34:27.520 --> 34:31.600
And now, I want you
to pay me back what you owe me.

34:32.400 --> 34:35.760
There is work you can do,
there are risks you can take.

34:36.520 --> 34:38.560
We were close before.

34:38.639 --> 34:41.000
Now, I want you closer still.

34:42.880 --> 34:44.960
Michael, honey,

34:46.560 --> 34:47.800
look at your cousin.

34:49.040 --> 34:50.560
He's in trouble. Huh?

34:52.400 --> 34:53.600
He needs you.

34:55.840 --> 34:57.199
Come on, baby.

34:57.280 --> 34:58.520
Let's go.

34:59.360 --> 35:00.760
[footsteps receding]

35:03.400 --> 35:04.400
[door opens]

35:09.640 --> 35:10.960
[car doors open and close]

35:14.360 --> 35:15.320
[car engine starts]

35:15.400 --> 35:16.960
-[door closes]
-[lock clicks]

35:18.240 --> 35:19.080
[car receding]

35:22.840 --> 35:24.560
[Arthur] Fucking cheek of her, eh?

35:26.480 --> 35:27.880
Mad Dog Jimmy...

35:28.400 --> 35:29.840
coming south.

35:35.080 --> 35:36.840
[Tommy] Not so mad anymore.

35:36.920 --> 35:39.480
He's got friends
in high places these days.

35:42.280 --> 35:44.480
A black cat dream is never wrong, brother.

35:55.880 --> 35:56.800
[horse whinnies]

36:32.640 --> 36:33.680
[gunshot]

36:33.760 --> 36:34.680
[groans]

36:34.760 --> 36:35.600
-[birds fluttering]
-[crow cawing]

36:36.840 --> 36:41.200
♪ Hello, hello, we are the Billy Boys ♪

36:41.280 --> 36:45.200
♪ Hello, hello, we are the Billy Boys ♪

36:45.280 --> 36:47.560
♪ We're up to our knees in Fenian blood ♪

36:47.640 --> 36:49.640
♪ Surrender or you'll die ♪

36:49.720 --> 36:52.840
♪ We are the Brigton Derry Billy Boys ♪

36:56.720 --> 36:58.800
Drop the pea shooter, son.

37:04.000 --> 37:07.800
A broken broom
stops all Gypsy curses, Mr Gold.

37:08.360 --> 37:09.720
[grunting and groaning]

37:11.560 --> 37:12.640
[coughs]

37:13.280 --> 37:14.600
Who the fuck are you?

37:14.680 --> 37:16.480
[McCavern] Did you not hear my song?

37:17.560 --> 37:20.280
These gentlemen are the Billy Boys.

37:23.440 --> 37:24.840
And me?

37:29.040 --> 37:29.880
I'm Jimmy.

37:29.960 --> 37:31.440
-[grunts]
-No! Fuck.

37:32.120 --> 37:33.040
[grunts]

37:33.120 --> 37:36.280
Good. Mouth broke so you can't talk.

37:37.400 --> 37:39.200
But you don't need to.

37:39.280 --> 37:41.960
-Your body will be the lesson.
-[Aberama groaning]

37:43.880 --> 37:49.200
You work in a particular capacity
for Mr Thomas Shelby OBE, am I right?

37:51.640 --> 37:52.480
[sniffles]

37:53.000 --> 37:53.960
[breathing heavily]

37:56.680 --> 37:57.640
I heard you're a fighter.

37:59.880 --> 38:01.120
The best.

38:03.480 --> 38:05.080
But your fighting days are over.

38:06.400 --> 38:07.560
[grunting]

38:08.120 --> 38:10.560
Because I need Mr Shelby to understand...

38:10.640 --> 38:11.840
[groans]

38:12.920 --> 38:14.160
-...that his best...
-[Aberama] Fuck.

38:15.760 --> 38:16.960
...is not...

38:18.000 --> 38:19.160
good enough.

38:19.240 --> 38:20.840
-[grunts]
-[muffled yelling]

38:54.360 --> 38:55.520
[grunting]

38:57.240 --> 38:58.240
[breathing heavily]

39:01.040 --> 39:01.880
[grunting]

39:10.960 --> 39:11.840
Bonnie.

39:12.360 --> 39:14.480
[McCavern] Farewell, fighter boy.
You died well.

39:15.880 --> 39:17.040
[horse neighs]

39:19.360 --> 39:20.280
[breathing shakily]

39:25.520 --> 39:26.520
[sobbing] Bonnie.

39:28.120 --> 39:29.160
Bonnie!

39:42.680 --> 39:46.000
Tell Thomas Shelby
it's time to fucking share.

39:48.200 --> 39:51.240
We'll take all the tracks south
as far as Nottingham.

39:51.800 --> 39:53.480
We'll take Cheltenham as well.

39:54.800 --> 39:58.760
Otherwise, it will be
Thomas Shelby who's crucified,

39:59.320 --> 40:01.080
and there will be no resurrection.

40:01.160 --> 40:02.040
[grunting angrily]

40:02.120 --> 40:05.000
[groaning and coughing]

40:05.080 --> 40:06.440
Come on, boys.

40:22.240 --> 40:23.200
[sobbing]

40:27.320 --> 40:31.720
[Billy] ♪ The sun comes shining through ♪

40:31.800 --> 40:37.160
♪ But when you're crying
You bring out the rain ♪

40:37.240 --> 40:39.640
♪ So stop your crying... ♪

40:39.720 --> 40:40.680
[music stops]

40:52.160 --> 40:54.920
Ladies and gentlemen, I'm just gonna
take a short break. Thank you.

40:55.760 --> 40:56.800
Yeah.

41:04.720 --> 41:07.320
Beautiful, Billy. Beautiful.

41:07.400 --> 41:09.160
Really nice. Really nice.

41:13.440 --> 41:16.160
Really meaningful,
you know, a heartfelt song.

41:16.840 --> 41:19.200
I like it. I really do.

41:20.440 --> 41:21.400
Boys...

41:22.680 --> 41:24.400
this here is Billy Grade.

41:25.160 --> 41:27.280
Man I was telling you about.

41:28.680 --> 41:30.720
Billy, this here's my kid brother, Finn.

41:30.800 --> 41:31.640
Hey.

41:33.040 --> 41:34.680
Have a drink, Billy.

41:35.680 --> 41:36.840
I can't, my voice is...

41:38.000 --> 41:39.280
Drink, Bill.

41:39.840 --> 41:40.680
Yeah.

41:41.720 --> 41:42.920
Yeah.

41:48.520 --> 41:49.840
You boys won't remember,

41:51.000 --> 41:54.840
but I remember when Billy here
made a living on the football pitch.

41:54.920 --> 41:55.960
[Billy laughs]

41:56.560 --> 41:58.800
Yeah, that was
a long time ago, Mr Shelby.

41:58.880 --> 42:00.200
-Yeah. What a left foot, eh?
-Yeah.

42:00.280 --> 42:01.360
[both chuckle]

42:01.800 --> 42:02.760
[Arthur] And then what?

42:03.880 --> 42:05.160
Manager, right?

42:05.720 --> 42:06.840
-Hmm?
-[chuckles]

42:07.320 --> 42:09.320
Well, yeah. And now I'm a singer.

42:09.400 --> 42:10.520
Are ya?

42:11.760 --> 42:14.240
Every football team in England...

42:15.240 --> 42:17.200
knows Billy Grade,

42:17.280 --> 42:20.840
and he knows a few people, too.
Didn't you, Bill, eh? Hmm?

42:20.920 --> 42:21.800
One or two.

42:21.880 --> 42:22.760
Useful.

42:24.240 --> 42:25.680
Very useful.

42:27.040 --> 42:29.640
But what do you do, Bill, eh? Hmm?

42:30.440 --> 42:35.480
You're in here, singing,
or whatever the fuck you call it,

42:35.560 --> 42:38.320
in shithole pubs in Birmingham.

42:38.400 --> 42:39.320
[tutting]

42:41.040 --> 42:43.640
That's no way to make a living, boys.

42:44.960 --> 42:46.840
-[Arthur] Degrading.
-[Billy] I love it.

42:47.800 --> 42:49.360
I really do, I love it.

42:50.240 --> 42:53.680
And thank you,
by the way, for inviting me here tonight.

42:53.760 --> 42:55.000
I really appreciate it.
So, thank you very--

42:55.080 --> 42:56.720
[Arthur] Don't thank me.

42:57.280 --> 42:59.280
I didn't invite you here to sing.

43:01.040 --> 43:03.840
I wanna listen to music,
I'll buy an Al Jolson record.

43:04.320 --> 43:05.160
Hmm?

43:05.640 --> 43:06.960
That's what I'd do.

43:08.000 --> 43:09.800
Real singer, ya know?

43:10.960 --> 43:13.080
Melody, tune.

43:14.080 --> 43:14.960
[stammers]

43:15.600 --> 43:18.240
So, what is it that you want, exactly?

43:22.240 --> 43:26.120
Finn will explain
the nature of my proposition.

43:27.360 --> 43:29.480
You'll listen to him, won't you, Bill, eh?

43:29.560 --> 43:31.000
You'll be attentive, won't ya?

43:31.080 --> 43:32.160
Yeah, of course. Of course.

43:32.240 --> 43:33.360
[Arthur] 'Cause Isiah here,

43:33.920 --> 43:37.280
he'll show you the fucking consequences
if you don't.

43:39.320 --> 43:40.160
All right.

43:43.920 --> 43:45.800
I'll leave you with the bottle. Hmm?

44:00.800 --> 44:01.960
What proposition?

44:03.360 --> 44:05.320
Right. What I want from you, Billy,

44:05.400 --> 44:09.840
is for you to write down
a name and a number

44:09.920 --> 44:12.600
next to every one
of those football teams, yeah?

44:12.680 --> 44:14.400
-Why?
-Why?

44:14.480 --> 44:16.600
People like to bet
on those kind of things these days.

44:16.680 --> 44:18.880
-We're a gambling enterprise.
-I know who you are.

44:18.960 --> 44:20.400
To fix a horse race,

44:21.160 --> 44:22.600
you give the outsider a bit of cocaine.

44:22.680 --> 44:24.600
-Jesus.
-To fix a football match,

44:24.680 --> 44:26.480
you give the goalkeeper 20 pounds.

44:32.680 --> 44:33.680
[chuckles nervously]

44:38.800 --> 44:41.000
You're a Peaky Blinder now, Billy.

44:41.680 --> 44:42.520
Hmm?

44:50.880 --> 44:52.200
[Arthur] What have you got there?

44:54.680 --> 44:56.000
[Linda] I've written a letter.

44:56.080 --> 44:56.920
Ah.

45:00.400 --> 45:01.920
Who for?

45:02.000 --> 45:03.000
For you.

45:03.920 --> 45:05.520
And Lizzie's written one to Tommy.

45:07.920 --> 45:09.880
[smacks lips] Well...

45:11.320 --> 45:12.360
can I read it?

45:12.840 --> 45:14.120
It's not finished yet.

45:14.920 --> 45:17.600
I'm getting rid of the parts I wrote
when I was drunk.

45:18.720 --> 45:20.400
By the way, I stopped drinking.

45:21.160 --> 45:23.640
And your bottles of snow
I poured down the lavatory.

45:25.400 --> 45:28.880
When I was drunk, I was too hard on you.
It's not your fault.

45:34.160 --> 45:35.160
So...

45:37.520 --> 45:39.240
that letter's about me, is it?

45:39.320 --> 45:40.400
Yeah.

45:41.560 --> 45:42.400
Hmm.

45:42.480 --> 45:43.760
And about me.

45:44.680 --> 45:46.800
About the future, about the company.

45:48.840 --> 45:49.680
Lizzie and I--

45:49.760 --> 45:53.080
Sat here and made things worse
the last few hours, hmm?

45:53.160 --> 45:54.040
Yeah.

45:54.120 --> 45:55.600
And we've come up with a plan.

45:55.680 --> 45:57.320
You've come up with a plan, huh?

45:57.400 --> 45:59.240
Lizzie says Tommy won't live
two more years

45:59.320 --> 46:00.960
if he carries on like this.
He's gone too far.

46:01.040 --> 46:03.840
Is that was Lizzie says, hmm? Really, now?

46:03.920 --> 46:06.960
Well, how far has he gone,
hmm, Linda? How far?

46:07.040 --> 46:08.960
He's lost all the legitimate money
in America.

46:09.040 --> 46:11.360
No. No, that was Michael.

46:11.440 --> 46:14.360
He's fixing races, he's fixing football.

46:14.440 --> 46:15.920
Following the financial crisis,

46:16.000 --> 46:20.800
the Shelby Company Limited has to find
other sources of cash income.

46:20.880 --> 46:22.800
Tommy went into Chinatown.

46:22.880 --> 46:25.880
He's selling out the communists
to the British intelligence.

46:26.480 --> 46:28.960
And all the time, every day,
he gets more and more famous.

46:29.040 --> 46:32.000
But that's okay, because if anyone
puts two and two together...

46:33.000 --> 46:33.920
[Arthur] That wasn't us.

46:34.000 --> 46:35.000
[chuckles sarcastically]

46:35.080 --> 46:35.920
It's not fucking us!

46:36.000 --> 46:39.280
It's going to blow up, Arthur!
It can't sustain. You know it!

46:39.360 --> 46:40.960
Oh, yeah? And what do you know?

46:41.520 --> 46:45.080
You've worked it all out,
you and fuckin' Lizzie. Huh?

46:45.160 --> 46:47.440
Got it all planned out, is that right?

46:47.520 --> 46:48.360
Hmm?

46:49.200 --> 46:54.800
I tell you, all you're gonna do
is you're gonna be a good fuckin' wife.

46:55.600 --> 46:58.880
Yeah, like the perfect couple,
we'll go upstairs.

46:58.960 --> 46:59.960
Hmm?

47:00.480 --> 47:01.960
We'll go upstairs...

47:02.520 --> 47:05.000
Yeah. And we'll make love. Hmm?

47:15.840 --> 47:19.520
I spent my day writing two letters
and deciding which one to give.

47:21.400 --> 47:23.600
Looks like I'll have to
give the other one.

47:25.960 --> 47:27.160
What other one?

47:28.120 --> 47:30.080
What fucking other one?

47:30.160 --> 47:31.080
[breathing heavily]

47:33.280 --> 47:34.920
[Lizzie] What did you do with my letter?

47:47.160 --> 47:48.400
I burnt it.

47:50.400 --> 47:51.640
So did Arthur.

47:51.720 --> 47:53.160
[Tommy clicks tongue and exhales]

47:53.720 --> 47:55.960
-Did you read it first?
-Yes.

47:57.320 --> 47:58.880
That's more than Arthur did.

48:01.000 --> 48:01.840
[grunts]

48:01.920 --> 48:02.760
[drawer opens]

48:03.480 --> 48:04.440
[drawer closes]

48:04.520 --> 48:06.680
Didn't help that you can't fucking spell.

48:08.320 --> 48:09.960
I left school too early.

48:11.160 --> 48:13.240
Did you read the bit about the lawyers?

48:13.320 --> 48:14.600
Do you wanna fuck?

48:15.800 --> 48:17.040
Didn't think so.

48:19.600 --> 48:21.400
-You don't want to eat?
-No.

48:22.240 --> 48:24.000
-You've got calls?
-Yeah.

48:31.680 --> 48:32.520
[exhales]

48:32.600 --> 48:34.840
It's Ruby's birthday today, Tommy.

48:38.040 --> 48:40.040
Do you know why I took her to Arthur's?

48:40.960 --> 48:43.200
Because she said she's scared of you.

48:44.400 --> 48:47.680
When she knows you're not coming home,
she's a different kid.

48:49.280 --> 48:51.960
But I've bought a cake,
and I want you there.

48:53.520 --> 48:54.840
We're in the drawing room.

48:55.320 --> 48:56.280
[footsteps receding]

48:59.000 --> 49:00.000
Lizzie.

49:01.960 --> 49:02.800
[footsteps stop]

49:05.720 --> 49:07.080
I'm in a room,

49:08.400 --> 49:10.720
and they're coming at me.

49:12.640 --> 49:14.640
But it's okay. I want 'em to.

49:16.160 --> 49:17.920
Last thing I want is silence.

49:20.280 --> 49:23.200
Standing up there in silence,
and someone says...

49:25.200 --> 49:26.040
[scoffs]

49:26.120 --> 49:28.600
"Sorry about all that noise.

49:28.680 --> 49:30.280
Sorry about all that...

49:31.200 --> 49:32.240
dust.

49:33.120 --> 49:35.200
Sorry about all that mud

49:35.280 --> 49:37.520
and all that fucking blood."

49:38.880 --> 49:40.720
And you say, "Don't be sorry.

49:41.640 --> 49:43.720
Don't be sorry. It's all I can do now."

49:48.520 --> 49:50.200
You want me to write this down?

49:52.760 --> 49:55.040
Do you want me to write you
a fucking letter?

49:57.440 --> 49:59.440
Me and Arthur can't write it down...

50:00.760 --> 50:03.400
'cause they haven't invented
the fucking words.

50:04.840 --> 50:05.760
[chair scrapes]

50:07.160 --> 50:09.400
We don't have the fucking words.

50:09.480 --> 50:10.640
[footsteps]

50:12.560 --> 50:14.200
And the worst thing is...

50:16.040 --> 50:17.760
could've stayed at school,

50:18.840 --> 50:20.360
but we volunteered.

50:23.200 --> 50:25.400
Still don't have the fucking words.

50:34.400 --> 50:36.480
Should you choose to depart, Tommy,

50:36.560 --> 50:39.080
either by your own hand or someone else's,

50:39.160 --> 50:41.480
the person who would
take your place is me.

50:42.640 --> 50:46.600
Legally, financially, everything.

50:48.040 --> 50:50.200
I need to know
there will be something left.

50:50.880 --> 50:54.320
Well, you know, Lizzie, in my head,
I still pay you for it. So...

50:55.480 --> 50:56.880
good luck with me.

50:58.440 --> 50:59.640
[phone ringing]

51:05.080 --> 51:06.240
I have business.

51:15.200 --> 51:16.040
[door opens]

51:17.080 --> 51:17.920
[door closes]

51:31.200 --> 51:35.200
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪ 

51:35.280 --> 51:38.680
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

51:38.760 --> 51:40.760
Yeah, I wanna ask you some questions

51:42.000 --> 51:44.040
about the night you met Michael Gray.

51:51.480 --> 51:52.720
Make a wish.

51:53.240 --> 51:54.320
Yay!

52:08.280 --> 52:10.040
[engine revving and accelerating]

52:17.440 --> 52:18.320
[engine revs]

52:20.120 --> 52:22.000
Okay, kids, come on. Let's go to bed.

52:22.080 --> 52:23.840
-Quickly.
-Why? Who's coming?

52:23.920 --> 52:26.720
That's the thing, Charles.
We don't know. We never know.

52:46.200 --> 52:47.120
[groans]

52:48.240 --> 52:49.720
[Dogs] Tommy!

52:52.080 --> 52:54.040
-Out of the fucking car.
-[Dogs] Don't!

52:54.120 --> 52:56.440
Get out of the fucking car now,

52:56.520 --> 52:57.880
or I'll open fire!

53:06.520 --> 53:08.560
[Aberama] You looking for traitors?

53:08.640 --> 53:10.160
There's one,

53:11.240 --> 53:12.880
-with his ribs mashed up!
-[sobbing]

53:12.960 --> 53:15.480
The man's gone fucking mad, Tom!

53:17.280 --> 53:18.360
You did this?

53:18.440 --> 53:20.280
[Aberama] With one arm and a hammer,

53:21.480 --> 53:25.440
and a mighty pain, and a mighty fury!

53:28.320 --> 53:29.880
They killed him.

53:32.000 --> 53:33.400
My son.

53:34.760 --> 53:37.560
They shot him and they put him up
on a fucking cross,

53:37.640 --> 53:39.160
and he's fucking dead!

53:40.400 --> 53:41.520
Who did?

53:55.120 --> 53:57.920
[Aberama] Only Johnny Dogs and his kin
knew where we were camped.

53:58.000 --> 53:59.520
[Dogs sobbing] No, Tom.

53:59.600 --> 54:01.600
-No, I swear to God, I never told...
-I'll fucking kill you!

54:01.680 --> 54:04.040
-[Dogs] I never told a--
-[Aberama] Fucking shoot him!

54:04.120 --> 54:09.120
-My only fucking son! My fucking only...
-[Tommy] Johnny! Johnny!

54:09.200 --> 54:10.760
[Aberama] Fucking took him from me!

54:12.520 --> 54:14.280
-[Aberama] My only son!
-[Tommy] It's shattered!

54:14.360 --> 54:16.960
-Listen to me. Listen to me!
-[sobbing]

54:17.920 --> 54:19.840
Your shoulder is shattered.

54:19.920 --> 54:21.560
You don't get it fixed,
you'll lose your arm.

54:21.640 --> 54:25.800
He's gone. They fucking killed him,
my only fucking son!

54:25.880 --> 54:27.640
I'll fucking kill you!

54:27.720 --> 54:28.640
[Tommy] Listen to me!

54:29.840 --> 54:33.000
How can a one-armed man
avenge the death of his son, eh?

54:39.680 --> 54:41.400
They crucified my son...

54:43.480 --> 54:44.720
for you.

54:49.480 --> 54:50.960
[grunts]

54:53.880 --> 54:56.040
[Lizzie] Get away from my house!

54:56.120 --> 54:57.120
All of you!

54:58.120 --> 55:00.320
Get away from my child!

55:01.000 --> 55:03.320
This is my house.

55:04.120 --> 55:05.640
And I don't want you back.

55:05.720 --> 55:08.080
I don't want you back!

55:18.640 --> 55:19.600
[bullets clattering]

55:26.200 --> 55:28.080
You wanna take on the Billy Boys?

55:28.160 --> 55:29.120
You need me alive.

55:31.920 --> 55:33.600
Everyone fucking needs me.

55:36.600 --> 55:37.440
[groans]

55:38.160 --> 55:39.960
Call an ambulance

55:40.040 --> 55:41.760
or a man will lose his arm.

55:54.680 --> 55:55.640
[sobbing]

56:01.200 --> 56:02.360
[Tommy] Come on, Johnny!

56:03.880 --> 56:04.720
Come on.

56:04.800 --> 56:05.800
[grunts and groans]

56:08.080 --> 56:08.920
[Dogs] Tom.

56:11.240 --> 56:12.800
I'm no black cat, Tom.

56:13.480 --> 56:15.320
I know, Johnny. I know.

56:17.200 --> 56:19.960
In all the world, of all of the people,

56:20.040 --> 56:21.960
you alone I know I can trust.

56:28.520 --> 56:30.520
[theme song playing]

56:44.800 --> 56:48.880
♪ On a gathering storm
Comes a tall handsome man ♪

56:48.960 --> 56:53.600
♪ In a dusty black coat
With a red right hand ♪

57:01.360 --> 57:05.840
♪ A shadow is cast wherever he stands ♪
